      "mergeID": "5ce09f85407ecb11a04158ff",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Reversing your api is not forbidden, so I and some of my friends made third-party applications and browser extensions to send text messages to other users. Some people can't communicate with voice physically, so these applications helped them to communicate with others.\n\nBut, VRChat developers have blocked the ways we sent messages. 10 days ago you blocked sendin with `/user/[USERID]/notification` and `type=message` (or `type=broadcast`). Me and my friends found new way to send messages (`/user/[USERID]/message`), that has worked till today. About an hour ago (about 2019/05/18 18:40 UTC) that endpoint started returning 404 error (not found).\n\nWhy you do this? You don't want your users to communicate? Or what? We need new method of sending messages.\n\nI post this in bug reports just because I think it is a bug. Even if you don't implement message system in your application, please don't remove the working ways in API, so third-party developers can use them.\n\nVersion: any (API bug)\nSteps: try to send text message to other user with API",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Broken messages with API",
